@bank all
// Head writer 4: being ill (the user's design via the lead; the Career engineer's keys, claude/leave 0.60.6).
// Rarely, you wake up unwell; it gets worse through the day until you see the infirmary (Deck 3) or sleep it off.
// A sick day never uses leave and never counts against you. TEXTS are shown by the game (no tokens but {me});
// "title | body". The bug is never named as anything serious: "a ship cold", "the Wren sniffles".

== career.sick.card
- Feeling rough | You've woken up unwell. See the infirmary on Deck 3, or rest in your bunk.
- Under the weather | Your head's thick, your legs slow. Infirmary on Deck 3, or bed.
- Not right today | You're unwell. Infirmary on Deck 3, or sleep it off in your bunk.

== career.tip.sick
- Being sick doesn't use your leave. You're excused. See Rina in the infirmary, or rest.

== career.sick.worse
- Your head's pounding. Everything's slow.
- Your legs feel like wet rope. The infirmary's on Deck 3.
- You're doubled over. You really need the infirmary, or your bunk.

== career.sick.well
- You wake up clear-headed. Whatever it was, you slept it off.
- Better. Much better. Your bunk did the job.

== career.sick.cured
- The medicine's working. Your head clears and your legs come back.
- Already easier to breathe. Rina was right. Annoyingly.

// Crew who see you while you're unwell.
== sick.getwell
? tier>=acquaintance
- You look awful. Infirmary. Now.
- {sigh}. You're grey. Go and see the infirmary, would you?
- Are you all right? You don't look all right.
? tier>=colleague
- Ship cold? Everyone gets one. Infirmary, then bed. In that order.
- Don't you dare come to shift like that. Go and lie down.   #warm

// A friend comes and finds you while you're unwell and untreated.
== sick.nudge
? tier>=friend
- {nick}, you look terrible. I'll walk you to the infirmary. No arguing.   #warm
- Bed or the infirmary. Pick one. I'm not leaving till you do.   #warm
- You're not excused from being looked after. Go and see Rina. Please.   #warm

// The next day or two.
== sick.better
? tier>=acquaintance
- Colour's back in your face. Good.
- Better? Glad. You looked half-mopped yesterday.
? tier>=friend
- There you are. Properly you again. Don't do that to me.   #warm
